(footprint "microSD_TF-01A"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "aquabeacon")
	(generator_version "8.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "microSD / TF card socket, PUSH-PUSH (self-eject), Korean Hroparts Elec TF-01A = LCSC C91145 (JLCPCB assembly part). 9 contacts (8 signal + Cd) on 1.10mm pitch + 4 shell pads + 2 NPTH locating holes phi1.00 @8.00mm. All geometry extracted from the vector PDF of the official drawing (pcb/datasheets/microSD_TF-01A_KoreanHroparts_C91145.pdf, PCB Layout/Pattern Side view = TOP view) and cross-checked against the labelled dims: pitch 1.10, span 8.80, pad 0.70x1.30, shell pads 1.20x1.40 (contact side) / 1.20x2.00 (opening side), holes 8.00 apart & 2.81 from the left shell-pad centreline, 15.52 between the bottom shell-pad centres, 9.70 between shell-pad rows. Origin = centre of that 15.52 x (pad-row -> bottom-shell) pattern. Pin order matches the KiCad Hirose DM3AT footprint (pin1 rightmost, Cd leftmost, card opening at +Y). Pad 10 = Cd (card detect contact); the detect switch closes to the SHELL, so one shell pad is numbered 9 so the Micro_SD_Card_Det2 symbol (9=GND / 10=CD) nets out correctly. The datasheet puts the Cd pad only 0.155mm from the left shell pad (below the 0.2mm board clearance rule but above the JLC 0.127mm limit), so BOTH LEFT SHELL PADS ARE SHIFTED 0.08mm OUTWARD (x -7.75 -> -7.83) to give 0.23mm; the shell leg is a mechanical tab so this is harmless and keeps the rest of the board on the strict 0.2mm rule. Card inserted from +Y. Body 14.85 x 13.4mm, height 1.85mm above PCB.")
	(tags "microsd tf card push-push TF-01A C91145 jlcpcb")
